    "## Executive Summary & Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "This Google Colab notebook provides independent, reproducible verification of the completed **R2-N1 implementation** using the actual trained Protocol B Logistic Regression (LR-B) model from R2-M1 (`runs/r2/r2_m1_20261106T140611Z/model`).\n",
    "\n",
    "The primary objective is to verify that the **exact same audio recording bytes** produce **identical recording-level scores** across:\n",
    "1. **The Production CLI** (`python -m echoproof.cli predict --bundle ... --audio ...`)\n",
    "2. **The R1-N1 Authoritative Evaluator** (`aggregate_recordings()` and `aggregate_from_contracts()`)\n",
    "3. **The Streamlit Application** (`app/main.py` via official `AppTest`)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Methodological Scope & Parity Principle\n",
    "- **Plumbing and Parity Verification:** The audio used in this notebook is synthetic audio generated deterministically to produce multiple canonical evaluation windows ($n_{\\text{chunks}} \\ge 2$). It verifies bounded decoding, feature extraction, chunk scoring, and recording aggregation parity across all execution entry points.\n",
    "- **Detector Performance:** Real-world model detection accuracy, calibration, and generalization over genuine speech and TTS generators are evaluated in R2-M1 and sealed test protocols (R5), not in this integration notebook.\n",
    "- **Evaluator Boundary:** R1-N1 provides an authoritative chunk-scoring aggregation interface, not an independent raw-audio decoding pipeline. Evaluator parity is verified at its actual contract and aggregation boundary using chunk scores produced by the loaded LR-B model.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runtime Requirement:** Standard Google Colab CPU runtime (GPU optional, not required). Execute all cells sequentially from top to bottom.\n"
   ]
