    "This stage generates deterministic synthetic audio long enough to produce **multiple canonical evaluation chunks** and runs it through the shared inference pipeline (`src/echoproof/inference.py`).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Canonical Chunking Analysis\n",
    "- The canonical evaluation policy (`src/echoproof/data/chunks.py`) uses a **4.0-second window** (64,000 samples at 16 kHz) with a **2.0-second stride** (32,000 samples).\n",
    "- An audio file under 4.0 seconds produces only a single chunk.\n",
    "- Setting duration to **6.0 seconds** (96,000 samples) produces exactly **2 canonical chunks**:\n",
    "  - Chunk 0: $[0, 64000]$ (0.0 s to 4.0 s)\n",
    "  - Chunk 1: $[32000, 96000]$ (2.0 s to 6.0 s)\n",
    "- We assert that $n_{\\text{chunks}} \\ge 2$ and use the **exact same audio bytes** across all downstream verification paths.\n"
