    "The authoritative R1-N1 evaluation package (`src/echoproof/evaluation/aggregate.py`) defines `aggregate_recordings()` and `aggregate_from_contracts()`.\n",
    "\n",
    "> [!IMPORTANT]\n",
    "> **Architectural Boundary Clarification:** R1-N1 provides an authoritative chunk-scoring aggregation interface, not an independent raw-audio decoding pipeline.\n",
    "> The shared scoring boundary between evaluator and inference is:\n",
    "> 1. Canonical chunking: `eval_windows()` (4.0 s window, 2.0 s stride).\n",
    "> 2. Model chunk scoring: `LRDetector.score_chunks` via the loaded LR-B bundle.\n",
    "> 3. Recording aggregation: `mean_probability()` in `inference.py` == `aggregate_recordings()` in `evaluation/aggregate.py`.\n",
    "\n",
    "This stage tests the actual evaluator aggregation functions on the canonical multi-chunk audio using the identical LR-B model weights, confirming that the recording-level score produced by the evaluator matches the shared inference engine.\n"
   ]
